Z||000000||DaRkLoRD||09-01-2001||10:05 PM||||I bought a laptop over ebay, and after the auction I found out it's going to cost more to ship it here than it cost to buy it!<P>The charge for shipping to Canada is $45... but it's only $25 to ship to Alaska... are american shipping companies evil or just stupid???<P>anyway, is there anyone in the usa who's going to be coming to Canada sometime soon and wants to bring me my laptop? I'll pay all shipping, etc..<BR>I'm hoping to be at the GTA Fieros show on Sept 15th, if that helps.<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
Z||000001||Monkeyman||09-01-2001||10:09 PM||||Steve--You paid less than $45 for a laptop computer??  Who was the seller?  Fred Flinstone?  If you wanted an ancient laptop, you should have asked.  I've got one that I bought used back in the stone age I probably would have given you.<P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000002||beer_stud_21||09-01-2001||11:35 PM||||Is that all shipping or is some of that duty?  I occasionally ship wood from here to canada via USPS.  I always grossly undervalue it on the slip at the post office so that the customer wont have to pay lots of duty on it.  Only drawback is you cant insure it for its real value.  So far I havnt had anything lost in transit so it has worked out good.  If you want to risk it just tell teh seller to send it USPS and declare a very low value on it.  The combination of sending it USPS and low duty cost should make the shipping considerably cheaper.    I bought a new Apple iBook.  It shipped from Taiwan, then went to Alaska -&gt; Illinois, Cali, then to Hawaii..... Talk about the long way!  hehe.  <P>-Marlin||||reg||1
Z||000003||Master_Sushi||09-03-2001||07:40 PM||||"Who was the seller? Fred Flinstone?"<BR>HAHAHAH...<BR>LOL<BR>Funny  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||4
Z||000004||DaRkLoRD||09-03-2001||11:35 PM||||It's a 486 DX4-100 that I bought for my mom so she can send and receive email...<P>I just need to find some way to get it to Canada without paying more for shipping than the actual thing cost..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I will be at the GTA show on sept 15th, any americans coming want to help me out?<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
Z||000005||thomas_l||09-04-2001||11:35 AM||||It's just customs. I think the first $25 in value is exempt and you pay GST on anything over that plus a small fee for the customs broker. When you ship UPS or FedEx, you pay the duty in advance. If the seller you bought from ships USPS/Canada Post, I think they collect duty from the recipient. Either way it's a big hassle.<P>What you oughtta do is have that drop shipped to a friend, family, or PFF member in Detroit and carry it home in your trunk.||||reg||1
